  "working": "Let m_i = initial molality of HCl = 2.48 mol kg⁻¹. Let m_f = final molality of unreacted HCl = 0.732 mol kg⁻¹. Let Δm = m_i - m_f = 2.48 - 0.732 = 1.748 mol kg⁻¹ be the molality of HCl that reacted. The reaction Mg + 2 HCl → MgCl₂ + H₂ consumes 1 mol Mg per 2 mol HCl. Hence moles of Mg that reacted per kg solvent = Δm / 2 = 1.748 / 2 = 0.874 mol kg⁻¹. Assuming the solvent mass is 1 kg (molality is per kg solvent), moles of Mg added = 0.874 mol. Molar mass Mg = 24.3 g mol⁻¹, so mass of Mg = 0.874 × 24.3 = 21.274 g ≈ 21.3 g (3 s.f.).",
